##############################################################################
#  GENERATED alongside the counter schema. Do not hand edit.
#
#  THE NO LANGUAGE MODEL CONTRACT
#
#  The runtime agent has no LLM. It cannot read "materially above the quiet
#  baseline" and act on it. So every check in fault-model.n4l gets an
#  evaluable twin here: window in seconds, aggregation, comparison rule and
#  a numeric trigger.
#
#  The prose in the fault model is for the human reviewing the graph. These
#  fields are what the agent executes. If a check has no entry here, the
#  runtime must report it as NOT EVALUABLE rather than skipping it silently,
#  because a check the agent cannot run is a hypothesis it cannot settle.
##############################################################################

-Check evaluation predicates

 :: predicates, machine evaluable, runtime ::

 check: tail drop delta on the congested egress queue (winsec) winsec: 300
        "  (aggregate) aggregate: delta over window, per interface per queue
        "  (cmp-rule) compare: against the same aggregation over an equal length quiet window
        "  (trigger) trigger: ratio above 3.0 on at least one queue

 check: transmitted byte spread across ecmp members (winsec) winsec: 300
        "  (aggregate) aggregate: delta over window, per member interface
        "  (cmp-rule) compare: max member against min member within the same group
        "  (trigger) trigger: ratio above 4.0 with the minimum member below 10 percent of the maximum

 check: table utilisation against the manual capacity (winsec) winsec: 0
        "  (aggregate) aggregate: instantaneous read, per asic per resource table
        "  (cmp-rule) compare: against the capacity for the configured forwarding profile
        "  (trigger) trigger: utilisation above 90 percent of capacity

 check: optical receive power against transceiver minimum (winsec) winsec: 0
        "  (aggregate) aggregate: instantaneous read, per transceiver per channel
        "  (cmp-rule) compare: against the transceiver specified minimum, at both ends of the link
        "  (trigger) trigger: below the specified minimum at exactly one end

 check: cpu queue drop delta by protocol class (winsec) winsec: 900
        "  (aggregate) aggregate: delta over window, per protocol class
        "  (cmp-rule) compare: against zero across the window spanning the flap
        "  (trigger) trigger: any nonzero delta on the class carrying the flapping protocol

 check: frame check sequence error delta on path links (winsec) winsec: 900
        "  (aggregate) aggregate: delta over window, per interface on the path
        "  (cmp-rule) compare: against zero across the window
        "  (trigger) trigger: any nonzero delta on any link in the path

 :: predicates, evaluation rules the runtime must honour ::

 winsec: 0 (note) Instantaneous read. Safe to issue as a single get, because the underlying metric is a gauge rather than a free running counter
 evaluation rule (note) For any counter whose kind says free running, a single absolute read is not evidence. The runtime must take two reads separated by the window, or subscribe and difference, and must refuse to report a verdict from one sample
        "         (note) A check with no predicate entry is NOT EVALUABLE. Report it as such and leave the hypothesis open. Silently skipping it turns an unsettled hypothesis into an apparently excluded one
